WEBVTT

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.580
Savina comes here because she has a thing for Luciano.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:31.070
I suppose it's the pastime of a widow with time and money on her hands.

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:32.900
I guess.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:35.730
She used to be a violinist.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.180
Be careful around the steam.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.170
That beautiful woman?

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:44.830
Luciano pretends he doesn't notice.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:48.470
Man, what a waste.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:52.940
Maybe he plans to stay alone forever.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.480
That's not it at all, I bet.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:59.650
It's because he still loves his late wife.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:07.720
You too?

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:46.790
Secret Love

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:49.060
<i>This mysterious restaurant is on a road just a little ways from the center of Rome.</i>

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:56.180
Here.

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:57.040
Hmm?

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.020
I'm going to be in a concert.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:01.320
You know how to play an instrument?

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.400
It's nothing special.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.880
There will be a bunch of ensembles performing.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.200
Oh?

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:12.580
What?

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:16.100
I'm going to be busy with rehearsals until the concert,

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.280
so...

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:23.750
You aren't bored?

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:24.890
Not at all.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:27.250
I told you to stay quiet, in the back.

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:32.500
His mother is busy, so we don't have an option.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:36.320
Franci's a good boy, so we're happy to have him.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:42.880
Want something to eat?

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:43.790
Sure.

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:50.760
It's so good.

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:56.100
Signore.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.110
Yes?

00:03:58.110 --> 00:03:59.730
I'd like to extend you an invitation.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:09.440
I'm directing a group of children in a concert next week.

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.650
It's next Wednesday.

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:14.140
I do believe this restaurant is closed that day.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:21.760
I'd be delighted if you accompanied me.

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:28.680
You're single, aren't you?

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:33.880
I got some info on you from the other camerieres.

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:37.250
What do you say?

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:44.250
I'm sorry.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.280
I have a previous engagement.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:49.760
I see.

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:52.760
I'm envious of her.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:57.530
Take her to the show, if you want.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:58.970
Goodbye.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:01.250
Oh crap!

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:19.440
<i>For her to give him the tickets instead...</i>

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:34.310
Papa, I'll leave the tickets I mentioned here.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:35.140
OK.

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:40.630
I've been busy and don't have time to look after him.

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:43.620
I'm really grateful you're taking care of him.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.460
Don't thank me.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:48.230
Why don't we go get dinner sometime?

00:05:48.230 --> 00:05:50.240
The three of you should take your time.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:56.740
Franci, I'll make you a tasty snack.

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:57.910
Come to the kitchen.

00:05:57.910 --> 00:05:59.010
Sure.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.680
Ah. Nonno had the same tickets.

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:04.340
What?

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.540
Really?

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:08.660
He gets asked out too.

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:12.470
He's still young. There are plenty of good women for him.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:14.950
Oh?

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:16.470
What are you talking about?

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:23.260
It's been quite some time since your wife passed away.

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:29.060
She figured you might be lonely, so came over the house,

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:31.150
but I...

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:39.770
We all need love until the day we die.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.280
That goes for men <i>and</i> women.

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:00.940
What?

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:03.820
I'm kinda envious of Savina.

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:05.830
She's pretty and passionate...

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:09.030
I think she's really serious about you.

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:16.820
I think going on a date every once in a while isn't a bad thing...

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:19.360
How about you go on some dates yourself?

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:22.220
I'm getting impatient with you.

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:25.950
I'm trying...

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:27.990
Come here.

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:29.080
Huh?

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:31.930
Tickets to a classical concert.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:33.720
But these...

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.560
I've got tickets already.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:42.480
Don't do something tactless like going with another woman.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:43.480
What?

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:12.800
Yes, that one.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:16.860
Please let the other party know it's all settled.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:19.330
Yes. OK, then.

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:20.240
I'm counting on you.

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:25.570
It's nothing.

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:26.420
Yeah.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:28.270
Bye. Ciao.

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:30.150
I'll help you carry these.

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:31.450
Claudio!

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:33.510
Thank you.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:44.990
This is it.

00:08:56.940 --> 00:09:00.130
What are you doing? Come in.

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:01.740
Oh, right.

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:08.800
Put the groceries down there.

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:14.350
Well, I guess I'll get...

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:16.340
I'll put a pot of coffee on.

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:18.810
I won't, if you're in a rush, though.

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:20.280
One cup never hurt anyone.

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:22.770
Have a seat.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:46.580
Some of those things must bring back memories for you.

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:50.650
It's rude of me to look through your things.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:54.200
Not at all! We used to be married!

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:58.990
That's just like you to say that, though.

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:04.800
You haven't changed, not one bit.

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:15.580
To our new lives.

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:16.800
Salute.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:26.950
Say, isn't that the sweater I bought for you?

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:30.680
You don't wear it much, so I thought you didn't like it.

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:33.760
I was trying to take good care of it.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:35.910
It's a valuable keepsake.

00:10:42.020 --> 00:10:43.370
Gabrielle...

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:46.280
Yes, let me get a good look at your face.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:52.280
Being with you makes me want to get in trouble.

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:04.350
I should get going. We weren't married long, but I enjoyed it.

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:13.380
Ciao.

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:17.500
Take care.

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:28.770
How's my coffee?

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:30.030
It's good.

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:35.770
You made me coffee every morning.

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:38.560
It was delicate and hot.

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:42.810
I was grateful for each morning.

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:43.780
Huh?

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:48.270
I don't think I ever told you that when we were living together, though.

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:55.110
It's strange. Now that we're broken up,

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:57.400
I can say it.

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:03.670
Thank you. Bye.

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:05.270
Thanks for having me.

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:33.570
What's wrong, Nicoletta?

00:12:33.570 --> 00:12:36.400
Claudio seems depressed.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:38.530
Is that so?

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:41.500
Something happened to him, huh?

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:42.850
You think so, too?

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:05.090
If you aren't feeling well...

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:06.470
No, I'm fine.

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:09.350
We're both single. You don't have to be shy with me.

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:11.520
I appreciate that.

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:17.650
So, you plan to live alone forever, Luciano?

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:18.480
Hmm?

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:22.250
Sorry, I shouldn't have asked that.

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:23.500
How about you?

00:13:24.180 --> 00:13:25.510
I...

00:13:25.510 --> 00:13:30.130
I lost my life partner. You're in a different situation.

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:34.210
Time stops for the dead.

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:37.790
But if you go on living, things change.

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:43.190
Whether or not you ask for it, the clock keeps ticking.

00:13:52.550 --> 00:13:53.740
Claudio...

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:55.350
Yes?

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:58.030
Umm, err...

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:00.850
I...

00:14:01.870 --> 00:14:03.980
Umm...

00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:05.990
Err...

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:09.070
Claudio!

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:12.500
I'll always make time for you!

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:13.400
Huh?

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:17.040
If you ever need to talk about something that troubles you,

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:19.450
come running to my chest!

00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:21.720
I don't mean anything weird by that!

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:23.440
Oh, I know.

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:24.700
Thank you.

00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:31.550
Because we're friends, after all.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:32.590
That we are.

00:14:38.460 --> 00:14:42.330
I don't think Claudio will turn me down, but...

00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:47.370
Take her to the show, if you want.

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:54.000
I don't think I'll ever be as sleek as Savina...

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:38.820
That was pretty good.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:42.230
OK, I'll be back.

00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:43.320
Have fun.

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:50.410
Signore Cameriere.

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:57.790
That previous engagement... Was it with your grandson?

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:00.260
I was asked to watch him.

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:05.940
Oh dear. Here I was wondering what your lovely wife was like.

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:08.610
I'm relieved.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:19.720
Looks like I am without a rival.

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.160
Or am I mistaken?

00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:49.240
Is there?

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:57.960
Come here.

00:16:59.750 --> 00:17:02.350
Thanks for watching him today, Papa.

00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:05.670
Huh? Savina!

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:07.700
Hello.

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:09.170
Do you know each other?

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:10.480
Yes.

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:13.710
She's a regular at the restaurant.

00:17:13.710 --> 00:17:15.730
Wow, what a coincidence.

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:19.350
This is Nicoletta and Marina.

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:22.820
Nicoletta works in the kitchen at dell'orso.

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:25.960
Marina is Vito the cameriere's wife.

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:26.970
Nice to meet you.

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:28.250
Nice to meet you.

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:32.770
Sorry for coming with a woman.

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:38.360
Savina is the wife of the owner of the studio I attend.

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:43.630
She used to be a violinist, so she gives me lessons sometimes.

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:43.630
<i>What? "Wife"?</i>

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:48.770
<i>Huh? She has a husband? That means...</i>

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:47.720
It was a beautiful performance.

00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:49.610
Thank you, Savina.

00:17:48.770 --> 00:17:49.610
<i>What?!</i>

00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:53.350
We should get going.

00:17:53.350 --> 00:17:54.110
Ciao.

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:55.150
Ciao.

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:01.590
You knew I was married, didn't you?

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:07.590
I must have behaved differently from a widow, huh?

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:27.700
How was it? Did you enjoy yourself?

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:28.790
I did.

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:31.250
You didn't fall asleep like Franci, did you?

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:32.720
Of course not.

00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:38.830
Hey, was the person who invited you there?

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:44.340
Was Mamma always with you?

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:50.630
You have to wrap up now, right?

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:53.880
I'll take Francesco home, so just come get him tomorrow.

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:56.310
Thank you. I'll be over first thing in the morning.

00:18:56.980 --> 00:18:58.490
I'm going this way, too.

00:18:58.490 --> 00:18:59.550
Ciao.

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:06.130
How many years ago did Luciano's wife pass away?

00:19:06.130 --> 00:19:11.230
Nine years ago. Right after I found out I was pregnant with Franci.

00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:19.190
I'd think she was my Mamma being reborn, had Franci been a girl.

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:22.510
But, I'm glad I had a boy.

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:28.790
No one could take the place of my Mamma.

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:31.890
Or Franci, for that matter.

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:42.550
I've thought it would be good for him if he met someone, but...

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:46.770
But he's still in love with his wife, huh?

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:21.710
<i>Savina never came to the restaurant after that.</i>

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:26.720
<i>No one knows what happened to her adulterous feelings.</i>

00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:29.830
<i>Secret love...</i>

00:20:30.840 --> 00:20:32.420
<i>Requited love...</i>

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:35.800
<i>Both of them cause their share of problems.</i>

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:38.140
<i>But I guess they both can be called love.</i>

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:47.690
<i>Love takes all shapes and sizes.</i>

00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:15.980
The People of the Ristorante

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:05.300
It's not that he can't forget,

00:21:05.300 --> 00:21:07.760
it's that he doesn't want to forget, no?

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:14.000
Claudio!

00:22:55.000 --> 00:22:57.960
You don't want to forget it, no? The final episode, that is.
